{"type":"text","timestamp":1793600321483,"sessionID":"ses_e6518723fffehqEQtG0gZAcr0b","part":{"id":"prt_19ae8c925001b5w8A2Ec2d11ym_text-0","sessionID":"ses_e6518723fffehqEQtG0gZAcr0b","messageID":"msg_19ae8c925001b5w8A2Ec2d11ym","type":"text","text":"Done. Findings, written to `result.json` (with a fuller write-up in `incident-report.md`):\n\n**Incident: 2026-06-02 03:17:42 → 03:53:31, 35m 49s (35.82 min) down.**\n\n- **June availability: 99.917%** — 2,149 s of downtime out of 2,592,000 s (30 days). **SLO 99.9%: met**, but with only ~3.5 minutes of the 43.2-minute error budget left.\n- **Root cause:** `/data` filled to 97% (3.1 GB free, warned at 03:10). Autosaves hit `No space left on device`, the server became unresponsive, and ~40 watchdog restarts all exited 137 while the disk stayed full. It recovered within ~80 s of backup rotation freeing 38.2 GB at 03:52:10.\n\n**How I know it's right:**\n- Start/end use the README's exact definitions — \"first save error to the 'server ready' line\" — and I grepped all three logs for every ERROR/WARN/FATAL/ready line: there is exactly **one** FATAL, exactly **one** `server ready`, and one contiguous save-fail/restart sequence, matching the README's \"only one incident.\"\n- Ruled out red herrings: the 06-01 RCON auth-failed ERROR is noise (heartbeats and autosaves continue normally around it), and the long 00:48–02:08 autosave gap on 06-03 has continuous ~1-minute heartbeats (low-player night, not downtime).\n- Timestamps checked by hand: 03:53:31 − 03:17:42 = 35:49; recovery corroborated by `backup rotation freed 38.2 GB` immediately preceding `server ready`, and by normal player joins/autosaves after.\n\n**Assumptions stated:** full 30-day June as denominator (logs cover only 1–3, README asserts single incident); `minutes_down` is the exact 35.817 rounded to 2 dp — rounding up to 36 changes nothing (availability would still be 99.917%, SLO still met).","time":{"start":1793600309544,"end":1793600321483}}}
